00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.420
Matt Ridley is one of the best-selling
and best regarded science writers on the planet.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:12.030
He wrote recently that in the face of the Coronavirus pandemic we are about
to find out how robust civilization is,

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:16.540
and that the hardships ahead will be
like nothing we have ever known.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:20.240
I spoke with Ridley from his home in
northern England. His next book,

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.740
"How Innovation Works and Why it Flourishes in Freedom" will be published in May.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.180
We discussed why the Coronavirus caught
him by surprise,

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:34.960
when he thinks we'll be able to reopen the world economy, why Brexit is good for Europe,

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:38.480
and whether he believes that sustained innovation and progress

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.620
can take place in authoritarian countries such as China.

